{"title":"Descartes' Circle Formula","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Descartes' Circle Formula is a relation held between four mutually tangent circles. \n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Definition_of_Curvature\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Definition of Curvature</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Statement\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Statement</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Proof\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problems</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Definition_of_Curvature\">Definition of Curvature</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Descartes%27_Circle_Formula&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Definition of Curvature\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When discussing mutually tangent circles (or arcs), it is convenient to refer to the curvature of a circle rather than its radius. We define curvature as follows. Suppose that circle A of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/5/5f51b54576318cbb9dcd328a0ff444361cff9f0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> is externally tangent to circle B of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/0/cb01353fabf2257b6bde123ad5970eb7891a59b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Then the curvatures of the circles are simply the reciprocals of their radii, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b91ee4543517bf8785b61f0b796f399bcb95493f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{r_a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"18\" height=\"39\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/1/8f1e9c439cca5d86fa64f33b27aa1fba5989f683.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{r_b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"17\" height=\"39\" />.\n</p><p>If circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is internally tangent to circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, however, the curvature of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is still <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b91ee4543517bf8785b61f0b796f399bcb95493f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{r_a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"18\" height=\"39\" />, while the curvature of circle B is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/4/d0490da7144353f28a6d1926bdea88d6e1f9e172.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{1}{r_b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"31\" height=\"39\" />, the opposite of the reciprocal of its radius.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/0/a10298bb91d00b0aaace608317f8d041d7040165.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(200); defaultpen(linewidth(0.7)); draw(Circle(origin,0.5)); draw(Circle((1.5,0),1)); dot(origin^^(1.5,0)^^(0.5,0)); draw(origin--(1.5,0)); label(&quot;$1/2$&quot;, (0.25,0), N); label(&quot;$1$&quot;, (1,0), N); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, origin, SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, (1.5,0), SE); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"225\" />\n</p><p>In the above diagram, the curvature of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> while the curvature of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/4/f94615bc59e3ebcdc39715aa9864b8a03a34440e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(150); defaultpen(linewidth(0.7)); draw(Circle((1.25,0),0.25)); draw(Circle((1.5,0),0.5)); dot((1,0)^^(1.5,0)^^(1.25,0)^^(2,0)); draw((1,0)--(2,0)); label(&quot;$1/2$&quot;, (1.125,0), N); label(&quot;$1$&quot;, (1.75,0), N); label(&quot;$A$&quot;, (1.25,0), SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;, (1.5,0), SE); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"245\" />\n</p><p>In the above diagram, the curvature of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is still <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> while the curvature of circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Statement\">Statement</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Descartes%27_Circle_Formula&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Statement\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When four circles are pairwise tangent, with respective curvatures <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/b/a0b4e89e208848ab242ba5c3a5a29850abaa113c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1, r_2, r_3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/c/a7ce82c4f62f7e439d80be7f44293f527af4619b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />, then the following equation holds:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b65ebd77e3b53f7a75866f19d3fdd4a093972618.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r_1 + r_2 + r_3 + r_4)^2 = 2(r_1^2 + r_2^2 + r_3^2 + r_4^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"331\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/e/ace1fd76350a19ed13018724594c88379a52c55b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k_4 = k_1 + k_2 + k_3 \\pm 2\\sqrt{k_1k_2 + k_2k_3 + k_3k_1}.\\]\" width=\"334\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Descartes%27_Circle_Formula&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Waiting for the MAA to grant permission to avoid copyright issues...\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problems\">Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Descartes%27_Circle_Formula&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2025 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">2025 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017220930\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.022 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 127/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4678/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9131:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017220930 and revision id 282399. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}